    "title": "Even-Odd Tree Validation",
    "category": "Trees",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "problemStatement": "Given a binary tree, determine whether it satisfies the Even-Odd Tree property. Nodes at even-indexed levels must contain strictly increasing odd values, while nodes at odd-indexed levels must contain strictly decreasing even values.",
    "input": "\u2022 The first line contains an integer N. \u2022 The second line contains the node values. \u2022 The next N lines describe the binary tree.",
    "output": "\u2022 Print YES if the tree satisfies the property; otherwise print NO.",
    "constraints": "\u2022 1 \u2264 N \u2264 2 \u00d7 10^5"
